    "description": "Northstar Retail operates a Java HTTP API whose router exposes login, health, customer, order, and payment endpoints. Every route except login and health must accept either a browser session cookie or a mobile JWT, and token issuers are expected to change independently of business code. The API gateway currently passes requests directly to Spring controllers, so each controller checks credentials differently and several exceptional routes bypass checks. A GatewaySecurityComponent must verify credentials through replaceable SessionCredentialVerifier and JwtCredentialVerifier components, reject invalid or absent credentials, and place an immutable customer identifier and tenant identifier into request-scoped context before routing. The gateway must also preserve public-route exceptions without allowing controllers to override a failed decision. Operations wants one auditable place to observe every authentication attempt and rotate credential mechanisms without modifying controllers. The decision is where identity verification and request-context population should occur while keeping controllers unaware of credential formats.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose the request-processing location and component boundary that verify credentials for every protected route and populate request-scoped identity before controller dispatch, while preserving explicit public-route exceptions.",
    "notes": "Uniform credential verification with replaceable Session/Jwt verifiers and request-scoped identity population at the gateway (authentication-enforcer) is the decision; the sibling pipeline positions are near-misses."
  },
